    "done_when": "An anchored section with id triage-first-batch is added to docs/evidence/archive/open-work-is-capped-landed.html (create the record if absent, following the layout of docs/evidence/archive/a-refusal-is-about-the-work-landed.html). It holds one table row for each of these seventeen plans, and no others: a-brief-should-not-cost-what-it-names, a-crew-process-ends-with-its-owner, a-cutover-is-measured-against-its-baseline, a-dispatch-returns-without-its-worker, a-dry-run-must-resolve-what-the-real-call-resolves, a-follower-keeps-your-work-in-view, a-follower-outlives-its-monitor, a-landing-beat-needs-no-hand-edit, a-landing-record-never-conflicts, a-lane-can-say-where-it-stands, a-live-worker-can-be-reached, a-page-load-reads-each-file-once, a-placement-with-no-reservation-mints-one-per-worker, a-plan-is-reviewed-before-it-is-built, a-refusal-is-about-the-work, a-review-can-see-the-figure, a-review-dies-where-nobody-is-looking. Each row carries four things. First, the fraction of the plan's declared implementable sections whose deliverable is present in the code at main HEAD, read from the code by opening the files each section names, not from the plan's stored impl; the row states how many sections were checked and cites the file and symbol that shows each counted one present. Second, the coordinator session that last dispatched against the plan, read from the promotion ledger and live run pointers, marked live when a run for it is in flight. Third, a proposed disposition: keep, merge into a named existing plan, or close with a one-sentence landed summary. Fourth, a one-line reason. A plan whose sections are all present at head is proposed close, never keep. Nothing is closed or edited in any plan: this node writes only the evidence record. The section states the batch's keep count, so the lead can sum four batches against the locked limit of 25 pending plans. The manifest names the main HEAD sha the reading was taken at.",
